{"body": "Summary\nFix memory leak in Spark from AuthSessionCache when using Iceberg and ensure resources get cleanup.\nBackground\nI am using Spark Connect where end-users will be submitting their spark jobs/queries from their end into the remote Spark Connect server. These queries runtime can ranges from seconds to minutes and query per users can varies as well. Also, in this case, the end-users are the ones who are creating spark session and defined the connection info to Iceberg REST catalog. By default, Spark Connect server will cleanup idle sessions after one hour.\nWhat I found out interesting is the memory usage of Spark Connect is not able to get garbage collected after Spark Connect server killed the idle sessions after reached default TTL. After some debugging, this point me to ClassLoader from Apache Spark leak in AuthSessionCache.java from Apache Iceberg.\nChanges\n\nFixing the ClassLaoder leak in Apache Spark in AuthSessionCache.java\nThe existed ThreadPools.newExitingWorkerPool created a ScheduledExecutorService and registers a JVM-level shutdown hook. This hook can inadvertently hold a strong reference to session specific ClassLoader in Spark connect via the tasks it manages, which preventing them from being released. This change replaces newExitingWorkerPool with newScheduledPool which creates a thread pool with daemon threads. Based on my understanding, daemon threads do not block JVM from existing thus prevent the issue mentioned above.\n\nEnsure proper resources cleanup in catalogs\nCachingCatalog and SparkCatalog now implements java.io.Closeable which allows them to propagate the close call to the underlying wrapped catalog. This will ensure that any resource referenced by catalogs are properly released.\n\nReference\nJIRA for Apache Spark: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/SPARK-54367\nPR for Apache Spark: apache/spark#59952", "date": "2025-11-15T03:45:19Z", "hash": "sha256:9473b110292f37ce9721", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#14590", "meta": {"additions": 598, "association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "base": "main", "comments": 28, "deletions": 6, "draft": false, "files": ["core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/CachingCatalog.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/auth/AuthSessionCache.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/hadoop/TestCachingCatalog.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/BaseCatalog.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkCatalog.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkSessionCatalog.java", "spark/v3.5/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/TestSparkCatalogClose.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/BaseCatalog.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkCatalog.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkSessionCatalog.java", "spark/v4.0/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/TestSparkCatalogClose.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/BaseCatalog.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkCatalog.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkSessionCatalog.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/TestSparkCatalogClose.java", "spark/v4.2/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/BaseCatalog.java", "spark/v4.2/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkCatalog.java", "spark/v4.2/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/SparkSessionCatalog.java", "spark/v4.2/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/TestSparkCatalogClose.java"], "labels": ["spark", "core"], "last_commit": "2026-11-02T16:39:14Z", "n_files": 19, "number": 14590, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "requested": ["singhpk234", "nastra", "huaxingao", "pvary"], "reviews": [{"at": "2026-11-02T13:37:25Z", "by": "nastra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-02T13:39:01Z", "by": "nastra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-02T16:17:13Z", "by": "MonkeyCanCode", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-02T16:17:39Z", "by": "MonkeyCanCode", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-02T16:39:31Z", "by": "MonkeyCanCode", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-03T10:12:29Z", "by": "nastra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-05T12:35:40Z", "by": "adutra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-05T12:37:10Z", "by": "adutra", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-11-05T15:02:33Z", "by": "nastra", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "open", "thumbs_up": 1, "updated_at": "2026-11-13T14:16:17Z"}, "people": ["MonkeyCanCode"], "refs": ["gh:apache/spark#59952"], "source": "github", "title": "Spark: Fix ClassLoader leak in Spark caused by AuthSessionCache and ensure resource cleanup", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/14590"}
{"body": "Currently Iceberg Kafka Connector stalls when it receives bad records. This PR implements support for bad record handling as per the configurations.\nThe user will be able to skip bad record instead of stalling, log the bad records if required and publish bad records to DLQ topic.\nThe DLQ support was implemented using org.apache.kafka.connect.sink.ErrantRecordReporter provided by Kafka Connect framework itself.\nSupport for following Kafka Connect framework's configuration were implemented:\n\nerrors.tolerance: Behavior for tolerating errors during connector operation. 'none' is the default value and signals that any error will result in an immediate connector task failure; 'all' changes the behavior to skip over problematic records.\nerrors.log.include.messages: Whether to include in the log the Connect record that resulted in a failure. For sink records, the topic, partition, offset, and timestamp will be logged. For source records, the key and value (and their schemas), all headers, and the timestamp, Kafka topic, Kafka partition, source partition, and source offset will be logged. This is 'false' by default, which will prevent record keys, values, and headers from being written to log files.\nerrors.deadletterqueue.topic.name: The name of the topic to be used as the dead letter queue (DLQ) for messages that result in an error when processed by this sink connector, or its transformations or converters. The topic name is blank by default, which means that no messages are to be recorded in the DLQ.\n\nQuery engine\nKafka Connect\nCloses #16876", "date": "2025-11-18T16:59:33Z", "hash": "sha256:202e6347dd7824ebe33e", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#14618", "meta": {"additions": 181, "association": "NONE", "base": "main", "closes": [16876], "comments": 16, "deletions": 6, "draft": false, "files": ["kafka-connect/kafka-connect/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/connect/IcebergSinkConfig.java", "kafka-connect/kafka-connect/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/connect/channel/CommitterImpl.java", "kafka-connect/kafka-connect/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/connect/data/ErrorTolerance.java", "kafka-connect/kafka-connect/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/connect/data/IcebergWriter.java", "kafka-connect/kafka-connect/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/connect/data/SinkWriter.java", "kafka-connect/kafka-connect/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/connect/data/TestSinkWriter.java"], "labels": ["spark", "parquet", "core", "data", "flink", "docs", "build", "not-stale", "KAFKACONNECT"], "last_commit": "2025-12-16T08:23:58Z", "n_files": 6, "number": 14618, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "requested": ["findepi", "bryanck", "manuzhang"], "reviews": [{"at": "2025-11-20T02:54:54Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-11-20T02:55:15Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-11-20T02:55:53Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-11-20T02:56:49Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-11-28T11:11:08Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-11-28T11:13:50Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-11-29T14:27:13Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-08T15:03:33Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-08T15:11:52Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-08T15:14:16Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-09T05:56:54Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-09T05:58:39Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-09T11:51:35Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-13T16:01:44Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-13T16:05:54Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-13T16:08:59Z", "by": "manuzhang", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-16T08:25:44Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2025-12-16T08:29:01Z", "by": "devendra-nr", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "open", "thumbs_up": 6, "updated_at": "2026-11-02T03:50:34Z"}, "people": ["devendra-nr"], "refs": ["gh:apache/iceberg#16876", "gh:apache/iceberg#16876"], "source": "github", "title": "Kafka Connect: Error handling with DLQ support", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/14618"}
{"body": "The rewrite-all=true option incorrectly bypassed file group validation (filterFileGroups()), allowing single-file groups to be rewritten. This caused the commit phase to incorrectly handle file replacement, resulting in both old and new files being retained in the table metadata, leading to duplicate rows\nFixes #14667", "date": "2025-11-26T17:09:03Z", "hash": "sha256:b3a443b6742fdf8e0d08", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#14696", "meta": {"additions": 222, "base": "main", "closed_at": "2025-12-03T10:10:29Z", "closes": [14667], "comments": 3, "deletions": 1, "draft": false, "files": ["core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/actions/SizeBasedFileRewritePlanner.java", "spark/v3.4/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestRewriteDataFilesProcedure.java", "spark/v3.5/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestRewriteDataFilesProcedure.java", "spark/v4.0/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestRewriteDataFilesProcedure.java"], "labels": ["spark", "core"], "n_files": 4, "number": 14696, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "state": "closed", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2026-05-22T17:02:53Z"}, "people": ["hemanthboyina"], "refs": ["gh:apache/iceberg#14667", "gh:apache/iceberg#14667"], "source": "github", "title": "rewrite_data_files with rewrite-all=true producting duplicate rows", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/14696"}
